      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:11ouhmu'
    '|a||So there''s a cliff between now and every later week. Past it, the line is flat again.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ypd8h3'
    '|b||Two months out, both offers sit beyond the cliff, shrunk alike, so a hundred and ten still beats a hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:14wpdak'
    '|a||But when week eight arrives, the hundred is today, and the hundred and ten falls off the cliff: seventy-seven against a hundred.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:i4hpud'
    '|b||Edmund Phelps and Robert Pollak wrote this down in 1968; David Laibson made it famous in 1997. It''s called beta-delta, or quasi-hyperbolic, discounting.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1pv8f46'
    '|a||Same person, same tastes. Only the date of the choice moved, and the choice flipped.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1go3gdg'
    '|b||That cliff is all we need for the gym. Say Ida, a clerk at Harbourtown''s bank, plans a workout for Tuesday.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Illustrative numbers: it costs her ten in effort on the day, and pays back fourteen in health from Wednesday on.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kps4sa'
    '|a||On Monday, both the effort and the payoff lie beyond the cliff. Both shrink by beta, so fourteen still beats ten, and she plans to go.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:4k2f1b'
    '|b||Now it''s Tuesday morning. What does she do?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:l0je81'
    '|a||She goes, surely. Nothing has changed since Monday.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1g1tgtv'
    '|b||Tuesday morning, β = 0.7. Does Ida go to the gym?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:144cgbz'
    '|b||Let''s see what Tuesday''s Ida weighs.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||One thing has: the effort is today now, at full weight. Ten against fourteen times seven tenths, which is 9.8. She skips.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||And plans to go on Wednesday, because from Tuesday, Wednesday is beyond the cliff.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:pg5c8p'
    '|b||That''s time inconsistency: each day''s plan is sensible, and each day''s self overrules it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:9lrtkw'
    '|b||Above about seven tenths, the two Idas agree. At beta equal to one there''s no cliff, and nothing to regret.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Want the formula behind the two bars? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:r98mq4'
    '|b||Each day''s self counts today in full, and everything after times beta, on top of ordinary discounting, delta.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||With delta at one, Monday values the workout at beta times fourteen minus ten: positive for any beta.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:hidkoq'
    '|b||Tuesday values it at fourteen beta minus ten, positive only above ten fourteenths, about 0.71.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:3drwh5'
    '|a||So Monday''s Ida loses every Tuesday. Unless Monday sees it coming.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||If she knows her beta, she can tie her own hands: a bet with a friend, a penalty she''d hate to pay if she skips.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:dryrl6'
    '|a||Like Ulysses tied to the mast. People do buy such ropes: in the Philippines, about 28 percent of bank clients offered a savings account locked until their goal opened one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:mb38lx'
    '|b||The gym members didn''t. They bought the flat fee sure their future selves would go. The authors'' own reading is overconfidence: present bias you don''t see coming.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1jm4yo'
    '|b||But careful with the dollar example. When Ned Augenblick, Muriel Niederle and Charles Sprenger tested it, choices over money showed very little present bias.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ly6uni'
    '|a||That makes sense: money today isn''t fun today, it can sit in the bank. Effort you feel when you do it.':
